      >  only packets generated that have a secondary address as source address are routing
      >  updates. You can define up to 32 secondary addresses on a single interface."
      Syntax: `awplus(config-if)# ip address <ip-addr/prefix-length> [secondary] [label <label>]`

**The objective this case is graded against**, per the dispatch: *the subject is a secondary
address actually SERVING TRAFFIC, not merely appearing in `show ip interface`.*  So every limb
below is measured on the wire -- who answers ARP, and what crosses the DUT -- with the feature
baselined OFF first, removal proven, and reboot persistence proven.


4. THE INSTRUMENT, AND THE FLOWS
---------------------------------
`tools/arpleg.py` runs every leg: it starts tcpdump on each NIC named, sends a known count of
crafted frames from one of them, stops, and prints a grouped count with the Ethernet src/dst of
every flow.  `--answer IP=MAC --answer-iface <nic>` runs a background ARP responder so the DUT
can resolve the fictional hosts (this DUT does not learn a neighbour from a request it merely
answers -- group A's finding, recorded in tools/README.md).

Two kinds of leg, each with its own controls:

  **ARP legs** (eth3 only).  Three targets in every leg:
    172.16.10.1   THE SUBJECT -- the secondary address.
    192.168.10.1  THE PRIMARY -- instrument control; it must be answered whenever the sender is
                  in ITS subnet, so a zero on the subject is a measurement.
    172.17.10.1   NEVER CONFIGURED -- negative control; must never be answered.

  **Forwarding legs** (eth4 -> eth3, i.e. traffic arriving from elsewhere and destined INTO the
  secondary subnet).  Three destinations in every leg:
    172.16.10.5   THE SUBJECT -- a host inside the secondary subnet.
    192.168.10.9  THE PRIMARY SUBNET -- instrument control; must always cross.
    172.17.10.5   NEVER CONFIGURED -- negative control; must never cross.

TOOLS: tools/arpleg.py, tools/cfg.py, tools/ckcon.py, tools/ckyn.py, tools/ckreload.py,
tools/rc2cfg.py, tools/rcdiff.py.  `python3.8` for every tool on tb277.
Captures: /tmp/ckB/T43862/ ; console transcript /tmp/ckB/console-u2.log


